{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/783506-variation-on-the-great-hunt-involving-urshul","id":783506,"title":"Variation on the Great Hunt involving Urshul?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-10T10:28:46-08:00","id":783506,"title":"Variation on the Great Hunt involving Urshul?","content":"If someone wanted to modify the Great Hunt rite so that it would turn a pack member into an Urshul instead of Urhan how would you run it? I was thinking myself<br /> a) singular target instead of plural targets. The only question then would be how to restrict it so that it wasn't a way to just make it a Great Hunt using Urshul form; I was thinking change the rolls so that one is made every 15 minutes instead of every minute. That way it would take about an estimated hour and a half to three hours to cast the rite which, when combined with the duration, would limit the number of pack members it could be cast on.<br /> b) keep the Ban, Integrity breaking point for humans, duration etc. Basically reskin the rite so that the difference between it and the Great Hunt is the form taken, time taken to cast the rite, and how many pack members are affected.<br /> <br /> It came out of a discussion involving whether a rite would be possible that could give a pack member the healing ability of a werewolf for a set period of time. I'm very unsure what I think about that idea and my gut feeling is to feel more comfortable using a rite that would turn a pack member into an Urhan or Urshul for a hunt thereby giving them the healing factor of a Primal Urge 1 werewolf while they were hunting. If you have any opinions about that as well please let them be known.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4586-vedic","user":"Vedic","date":". 12-10-20